1
00:00:06,023 --> 00:00:09,659
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
Great Detective Conan
Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi

2
00:00:09,793 --> 00:00:11,895
This is... a bomb?!

3
00:00:11,962 --> 00:00:12,963
Eh!?

4
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:16,066
Ah! There's already
less than a minute left!

5
00:00:16,166 --> 00:00:18,068
There's no mistake about the time.

6
00:00:18,135 --> 00:00:22,172
Let's see, let's see... Ah! Was this that
occasion when those two came from Osaka?

7
00:00:22,239 --> 00:00:26,076
Still, there are several candidates
for the keyword to this one...

8
00:00:27,778 --> 00:00:30,947
Shin'ichi, say, are you really going home?

9
00:00:31,515 --> 00:00:34,317
That High School Student Detective
like you is coming from Osaka.

10
00:00:34,384 --> 00:00:36,186
- Don't you want to meet him?
- Fool!

11
00:00:36,353 --> 00:00:39,423
Anyhow, isn't Sherlock Holmes there
just an ordinary detective?

12
00:00:39,556 --> 00:00:40,824
So I'm really...

13
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:42,225
"Osaka High School Student Detective - Hattori Heiji"
...not interested.

14
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:44,127
Saying that again.

15
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:46,229
"Heiji's Childhood Friend - Toyama Kazuha"
Truth is, ya are worried 'bout him.

16
00:00:46,296 --> 00:00:47,864
Am not!

17
00:00:47,931 --> 00:00:50,700
I wouldn't even know his face.

18
00:00:51,068 --> 00:00:53,937
More importantly,
where's the bus to Teitan High School?

19
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:57,074
Even so, it's been going around recently that
"East is Kudoć, West is Hattori"...

20
00:00:57,107 --> 00:00:58,642
Huh?!

21
00:00:59,076 --> 00:01:01,878
Huh? When you say that, say,
"West is Hattori, East is Kudo"!

22
00:01:02,045 --> 00:01:05,348
Got that?
"West is Hattori, East is Kudo."

23
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:07,150
Get the order straight!
The order!

24
00:01:07,217 --> 00:01:08,685
See, you are worried about him!

25
00:01:08,752 --> 00:01:11,455
Am not, IDIOT!
Geez, you.

26
00:01:11,555 --> 00:01:14,124
What would I be doing worrying 'bout
some good-fer-nothin' anyhow?

27
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:17,394
He's been racking up cases
left and right here in Tokyo.

28
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:20,664
He's badder than you in Tokyo,
so you'd better keep up your guard.

29
00:01:20,764 --> 00:01:21,965
Fool!

30
00:01:22,065 --> 00:01:24,935
Who on earth's gonna
raise the tension here in Tokyo?

31
00:01:25,035 --> 00:01:27,604
More importantly Heiji, you've got
that lucky charm on you, right?

32
00:01:27,704 --> 00:01:31,041
When you forgot the charm that once,
ya got seriously hurt during the match.

33
00:01:31,074 --> 00:01:32,542
Kazuha, take these!

34
00:01:32,609 --> 00:01:33,543
Heiji?!

35
00:01:33,610 --> 00:01:35,812
Wait right there, ya brat!

36
00:01:36,813 --> 00:01:38,548
Wait!

37
00:01:38,982 --> 00:01:40,550
Wait!

38
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:43,854
Hey! Purse snatcher!

39
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,489
Wait up! Come here!

40
00:01:45,589 --> 00:01:46,990
What was that?

41
00:01:47,057 --> 00:01:50,193
At a time like this,
a good citizen should...

42
00:01:50,227 --> 00:01:51,495
"Shin'ichi's Childhood Friend
Mori Ran"

43
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:58,668
There!

44
00:02:01,238 --> 00:02:02,239
Ah! This is bad!

45
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:04,574
Ah...

46
00:02:05,575 --> 00:02:08,311
At a time like this,
what should a good citizen do?

47
00:02:08,411 --> 00:02:11,014
Fool! I know.

48
00:02:14,985 --> 00:02:16,586
Kyaa!

49
00:02:17,587 --> 00:02:18,688
Excuse me!

50
00:02:18,788 --> 00:02:21,258
Is anyone there!? Excuse me!

51
00:02:22,592 --> 00:02:25,195
There you are, Heiji.
Geez, these are heavy!

52
00:02:25,228 --> 00:02:27,364
Ah! Kazuha, take care of this guy.

53
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:29,366
Eh? Wai... Heiji!

54
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:37,007
Hey, pretty girl there! Could you stop
staring off into space and call the police?

55
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:38,475
Eh? Me?

56
00:02:38,575 --> 00:02:40,410
Hurry and call the police!

57
00:02:40,477 --> 00:02:41,912
"Fujimaru"
Excuse me!

58
00:02:44,915 --> 00:02:46,183
Damn!

59
00:02:49,653 --> 00:02:52,756
Bro, leave the rest up to me.

60
00:02:52,822 --> 00:02:54,491
Huh? What are you saying!

61
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:56,826
Well, it's okay.
Just keep quiet and watch.

62
00:02:57,394 --> 00:02:58,828
Excuse me...

63
00:02:58,929 --> 00:03:01,498
"Kazuo's Wife - Fujimaru Yoshino"
What business do you have with my home?

64
00:03:01,865 --> 00:03:03,733
You live here, right?
Just now there was...

65
00:03:03,767 --> 00:03:05,835
I heard a scream coming from your house.
I figure something must've happened.

66
00:03:05,869 --> 00:03:07,003
Hurry and go inside!

67
00:03:07,137 --> 00:03:08,405
Yes...

68
00:03:08,505 --> 00:03:10,106
Excuse me.

69
00:03:12,209 --> 00:03:13,977
What is it with this guy...

70
00:03:28,825 --> 00:03:30,560
The key's inside...

71
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:32,796
"Fujimaru Family's Detached House"

72
00:03:34,731 --> 00:03:38,034
Dear!
Hey! You're inside, aren't you?

73
00:03:38,335 --> 00:03:39,336
Dear!

74
00:03:39,369 --> 00:03:41,104
Who's inside other than your husband?

75
00:03:41,171 --> 00:03:43,540
His Assistant, Hideko-san...

76
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:47,377
Maybe they're so seriously hurt
they can't answer...

77
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:49,646
Hey! Dear!

78
00:03:49,679 --> 00:03:51,648
- Um, what sort of...
- Okay!

79
00:03:51,815 --> 00:03:53,250
I'll break down the door!

80
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:54,017
Huh?

81
00:03:54,050 --> 00:03:55,285
Here goes!

82
00:03:58,955 --> 00:04:00,457
Dear...

83
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,595
Dear...

84
00:04:05,795 --> 00:04:08,198
Could it be you and Hinako-san were...?

85
00:04:11,735 --> 00:04:12,902
Ah!

86
00:04:15,872 --> 00:04:17,407
Please calm down.

87
00:04:17,474 --> 00:04:19,409
Bro, get an ambulance.

88
00:04:19,843 --> 00:04:21,411
No...

89
00:04:23,113 --> 00:04:25,415
Make that the police.

90
00:04:33,423 --> 00:04:35,191
"Kazuo's Assistant
Nakashima Hideko"

91
00:04:44,334 --> 00:04:47,904
Fujimori Kazuo...
Occupation, Composer.

92
00:04:48,371 --> 00:04:49,339
Yeah.

93
00:04:49,439 --> 00:04:52,809
When your Assistant Nakashima Hideko
and you are working on writing music...

94
00:04:52,842 --> 00:04:56,479
"Beika Police Detective - Moria Masayoshi"
...do you always take the key to
the detached house from the entrance?

95
00:04:58,682 --> 00:05:03,253
What you call "writing music,"
is in reality a delicate thing.

96
00:05:03,853 --> 00:05:06,156
We didn't want to bother anyone.

97
00:05:08,525 --> 00:05:14,097
There was some broken glass on the sofa
that had fallen on Hideko-san.

98
00:05:28,878 --> 00:05:30,413
- Ow!
- Ow!

99
00:05:31,848 --> 00:05:34,684
Bro, don't loiter around so much!

100
00:05:35,051 --> 00:05:36,386
Look you, I was...

101
00:05:36,453 --> 00:05:39,022
Oi! You, schoolboy there!

102
00:05:40,724 --> 00:05:42,158
Yes?

103
00:05:43,626 --> 00:05:47,697
This soccer ball here is yours, isn't it?

104
00:05:48,098 --> 00:05:49,099
Yes.

105
00:05:49,165 --> 00:05:54,471
Fujimaru-san, did this ball
smash into that glass?

106
00:05:55,004 --> 00:05:56,673
Yes...

107
00:05:57,407 --> 00:05:58,775
That's it!

108
00:05:58,875 --> 00:06:02,545
I didn't recall it since it happened so suddenly,
but I think that's probably right.

109
00:06:02,645 --> 00:06:04,114
Hear that?

110
00:06:04,814 --> 00:06:07,817
It's your fault someone died.

111
00:06:08,017 --> 00:06:10,086
- That's wrong...
- Ya got it wrong!

112
00:06:10,553 --> 00:06:12,122
It ain't Bro's fault.

113
00:06:12,188 --> 00:06:13,656
What?

114
00:06:15,725 --> 00:06:20,663
The ball came in from above at this angle,
broke the window and struck against here.

115
00:06:20,830 --> 00:06:23,500
Look, you can tell.
There's traces of the ball here.

116
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:28,505
And then it lost momentum and stopped here.

117
00:06:28,571 --> 00:06:30,974
How can you say such a thing?!

118
00:06:31,174 --> 00:06:33,643
Take a good look around.

119
00:06:34,177 --> 00:06:39,182
If ya think about it, it'd be impossible for
the ball to come in and hit that glass.

120
00:06:39,949 --> 00:06:44,621
Thing is, the ball not only KO'd a purse snatcher,
it broke through this window.

121
00:06:44,721 --> 00:06:48,792
It didn't have the energy left
to break the glass in that frame as well.

122
00:06:48,925 --> 00:06:51,327
Moreover, the time lag between when
the ball broke the window...

123
00:06:51,428 --> 00:06:54,030
...and when the glass smashed was unusual...

124
00:06:54,164 --> 00:06:56,232
Enough's enough!

125
00:06:56,466 --> 00:06:59,068
What's this "time lag" stuff?

126
00:06:59,569 --> 00:07:03,239
Aside from being some dumb kids,
just who on earth are you?!

127
00:07:03,673 --> 00:07:05,542
You don't know? I'm...

128
00:07:05,575 --> 00:07:08,278
The name's Hattori Heiji.

129
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:11,948
Around Osaka, I'm kinda known as
the High School Detective.

130
00:07:13,216 --> 00:07:14,717
Detective?

131
00:07:14,884 --> 00:07:18,288
The ones I hate most are detectives!

132
00:07:18,455 --> 00:07:23,426
All they tell you is how great they are
and just what achievements they've made!

133
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:27,831
Just shut up! It's best to leave
this investigation to us police!

134
00:07:29,365 --> 00:07:32,068
Ah... excuse me!
We should go now.

135
00:07:32,101 --> 00:07:34,337
It's okay, it's okay.
Hey, Detective.

136
00:07:34,404 --> 00:07:35,705
A moment.

137
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:44,180
He's the son of Police Superintendent Hattori Heizo
of the Osaka Prefecture Police Headquarters?

138
00:07:49,018 --> 00:07:52,188
I didn't know!
I am truly sorry about that!

139
00:07:52,288 --> 00:07:55,425
I'm the MPD's Beika Police Office,
Crime Enforcement Unit...

140
00:07:55,458 --> 00:07:58,027
...Police Sargent Moria Masayoshi!

141
00:07:58,061 --> 00:08:00,497
Ya didn't have ta tell 'im who my father is.

142
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:03,933
It's okay!
If ya've got it, flaunt it.

143
00:08:05,435 --> 00:08:07,103
Well, whatever.

144
00:08:07,670 --> 00:08:10,573
Ah, let's see.
Bro, what's yer name?

145
00:08:10,673 --> 00:08:11,608
Ah...

146
00:08:11,641 --> 00:08:14,277
You're a detective and you don't know?
This is Kudo...

147
00:08:14,344 --> 00:08:15,845
Ahh! It's To...

148
00:08:15,945 --> 00:08:17,714
Just call me Toiru...

149
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:21,484
The "To" is like "Toguchi" (door), the "I" like "Italy"
and "ru" like "Nagareru" (to stream or flow),
so it's written as "Toiru."

150
00:08:21,551 --> 00:08:23,720
I'm just an ordinary 2nd year student
at Teitan High School.

151
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:27,557
Toiru...
That's a rare name, ain't it?

152
00:08:27,624 --> 00:08:29,392
Hmm... Toiru, huh?

153
00:08:29,492 --> 00:08:32,128
Well anyhoo, just leave the rest to me.

154
00:08:32,195 --> 00:08:34,130
If you would please.

155
00:08:37,834 --> 00:08:40,603
Hey, Shin'ichi!
What are you planning?!

156
00:08:40,670 --> 00:08:42,005
What's this "Toiru" thing?

157
00:08:42,105 --> 00:08:44,007
Shh!

158
00:08:44,073 --> 00:08:46,609
This is a rare chance, isn't it?

159
00:08:46,843 --> 00:08:49,178
Perhaps this isn't a coincidence.

160
00:08:49,345 --> 00:08:53,583
I get to take a look at
Osaka's Great Detective.

161
00:08:53,983 --> 00:08:57,086
The soccer ball didn't hit it.

162
00:08:57,186 --> 00:09:00,924
Then, how did the glass
in this frame break...

163
00:09:01,224 --> 00:09:03,226
There's that, ain't there?

164
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:06,429
That's the question.

165
00:09:06,529 --> 00:09:09,766
Anyhoo, this is a perfect closed room case...

166
00:09:09,866 --> 00:09:13,536
...where all the entrances
and windows were locked.

167
00:09:14,037 --> 00:09:18,808
Could've been set up by someone...
to make us think it was an accident.

168
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:20,310
Right?

169
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:24,480
What was that?

170
00:09:24,547 --> 00:09:26,015
Fujimaru-san...

171
00:09:26,249 --> 00:09:29,786
When we rushed up...

172
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:33,222
...why didn't you open the door right away?

173
00:09:33,590 --> 00:09:36,359
Ya should've answered your wife.

174
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:38,661
So why didn't ya?

175
00:09:39,228 --> 00:09:43,299
Ah, that was...

176
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:48,237
I was dumbstruck by
the suddenness of it all.

177
00:09:48,605 --> 00:09:50,206
Look, anyone would...

178
00:09:50,273 --> 00:09:52,175
I see.

179
00:09:52,275 --> 00:09:57,480
But... ya still had time to stop yer music.

180
00:09:58,615 --> 00:10:00,516
What do you mean?

181
00:10:00,984 --> 00:10:02,185
Ready?

182
00:10:02,285 --> 00:10:06,089
After Toiru's ball
broke through this window...

183
00:10:06,189 --> 00:10:09,592
...we heard some really loud music
comin' from this room.

184
00:10:09,993 --> 00:10:12,161
And then a little later...

185
00:10:12,261 --> 00:10:15,198
...we heard the sound of glass breaking.

186
00:10:15,264 --> 00:10:19,202
After Hideko-san's scream,
the music stopped.

187
00:10:19,535 --> 00:10:22,472
I'm asking who stopped it.

188
00:10:22,939 --> 00:10:26,342
Fujimaru-san,
were you the one who stopped it?

189
00:10:26,442 --> 00:10:29,078
I told you, since I was so surprised,
I don't remember!

190
00:10:29,145 --> 00:10:30,813
What's more...

191
00:10:31,514 --> 00:10:34,017
While you were listening to music
turned up that loud...

192
00:10:34,183 --> 00:10:36,886
...how could you possibly be doing
any composing?

193
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:43,026
That certainly ain't delicate, is it?
That kind of song writing.

194
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:46,029
That was...

195
00:10:46,062 --> 00:10:47,430
While you were working...

196
00:10:47,497 --> 00:10:52,101
...it's also strange yer Assistant
would be lying down on the sofa.

197
00:10:53,336 --> 00:10:54,837
Fujimaru-san...

198
00:10:54,971 --> 00:10:58,741
...truth is, you and Hideko-san
were on this sofa...

199
00:10:58,941 --> 00:11:01,077
Don't joke around!

200
00:11:03,813 --> 00:11:07,483
Ma'am, you said it when you
saw your husband, didn't you?

201
00:11:07,550 --> 00:11:10,286
"It couldn't be that Hideko-san
and you were..."

202
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:12,355
Could you tell me?

203
00:11:12,722 --> 00:11:14,657
The meaning of those words.

204
00:11:14,957 --> 00:11:16,359
Enough's enough!

205
00:11:16,993 --> 00:11:18,628
Be quiet!

206
00:11:19,462 --> 00:11:22,432
Yoshino, don't tell them anything!

207
00:11:22,632 --> 00:11:24,834
You don't have to say anything. Right!

208
00:11:29,505 --> 00:11:31,607
Detective, take care of the husband.

209
00:11:31,741 --> 00:11:33,509
Understood!

210
00:11:37,313 --> 00:11:40,950
"Fujimaru Family Main Wing, Living Room"

211
00:11:48,391 --> 00:11:49,826
Here.

212
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:52,428
Thank you.

213
00:11:55,998 --> 00:12:01,838
I didn't want such an ugly story
to come out like this.

214
00:12:03,239 --> 00:12:05,441
When did ya first notice it?

215
00:12:05,508 --> 00:12:07,910
Your husband and Hideko-san's relationship.

216
00:12:10,246 --> 00:12:11,948
About...

217
00:12:12,448 --> 00:12:14,884
...3 months ago.

218
00:12:15,384 --> 00:12:19,856
I'm sure he had just forgotten
to take in the key.

219
00:12:29,132 --> 00:12:33,503
He was only playing the music that loud
so their affair wouldn't be exposed, wasn't he?

220
00:12:33,636 --> 00:12:36,572
Ma'am, I feel so sorry for ya.

221
00:12:40,243 --> 00:12:43,012
You've been avidly watching him, haven't you?

222
00:12:43,112 --> 00:12:45,248
What? Are you jealous?

223
00:12:45,314 --> 00:12:47,784
Fo... fool! Who's jealous?

224
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:49,552
Then leave me alone.

225
00:12:50,052 --> 00:12:51,788
Ah... Eh?

226
00:12:51,954 --> 00:12:53,556
Ma'am, is that true?

227
00:12:53,723 --> 00:12:55,291
Yes.

228
00:12:55,525 --> 00:13:00,196
"I'll hurry and break up with her."
I heard him blame Hideko-san for it.

229
00:13:00,429 --> 00:13:03,266
"If she won't, I'll kill her," he said.

230
00:13:03,332 --> 00:13:05,268
A threat, huh...

231
00:13:05,334 --> 00:13:08,771
All right.
Ma'am, it's best if you wait here.

232
00:13:11,808 --> 00:13:14,110
Hey, little Sis there.

233
00:13:14,610 --> 00:13:16,879
Eh? You mean me?

234
00:13:16,946 --> 00:13:19,549
This guy Toiru-kun called you Ran.
That's you, right?

235
00:13:19,649 --> 00:13:21,017
Yes.

236
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:26,322
Could you come with me for a bit?

237
00:13:27,190 --> 00:13:28,925
Um...

238
00:13:29,725 --> 00:13:31,060
You want something of me?

239
00:13:31,093 --> 00:13:36,399
I'll say this especially, but if ya's makes
a pass at Heiji, I won't keep still about it.

240
00:13:36,966 --> 00:13:37,834
Huh?

241
00:13:37,867 --> 00:13:42,638
Long time ago, me and Heiji were in
a relationship like a "chain of iron."

242
00:13:43,372 --> 00:13:46,042
So if some pretty little thing
thinks she can come along...

243
00:13:46,142 --> 00:13:49,445
...and easily break that chain,
she's got another thing...

244
00:13:49,478 --> 00:13:50,913
Don't worry!

245
00:13:51,047 --> 00:13:54,250
I would never, ever do such a thing.
Rest assured about that.

246
00:13:54,317 --> 00:13:55,585
Then what was that?

247
00:13:55,685 --> 00:14:00,990
You could say he's got an atmosphere
about him similar to the one I think about...

248
00:14:01,224 --> 00:14:04,360
What's that? Are ya saying ya like
a man similar to my Heiji?

249
00:14:04,427 --> 00:14:07,964
No, it's not "like" or anything...

250
00:14:08,764 --> 00:14:12,335
You could say it's more like
being around a detective otaku is...

251
00:14:12,401 --> 00:14:13,569
Ah!

252
00:14:13,669 --> 00:14:15,771
He's like this huge loves-mysteries nut!

253
00:14:15,872 --> 00:14:18,808
Huh? A huge loves-mysteries nut?

254
00:14:19,041 --> 00:14:22,378
Yoshino-san, you helped
compose this too, didn't you?

255
00:14:23,446 --> 00:14:24,714
Yes.

256
00:14:24,814 --> 00:14:29,285
Before we got married,
I was Fujimaru's Assistant.

257
00:14:29,685 --> 00:14:34,357
Then I'm sure you must know
a lot about music, don't you?

258
00:14:34,857 --> 00:14:36,792
Not that much.

259
00:14:51,674 --> 00:14:53,776
Hold on a minute there.

260
00:14:53,943 --> 00:14:55,778
I've never threatened Hideko!

261
00:14:55,811 --> 00:14:57,346
My wife's mistaken...

262
00:14:57,446 --> 00:14:59,882
Anyhow, I wouldn't kill her!

263
00:15:00,016 --> 00:15:02,652
Then what's the reason you didn't
open the door right away?

264
00:15:02,818 --> 00:15:06,656
Like I said...
I told you I don't remember, didn't I!

265
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:14,630
Could it be you...

266
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:18,567
Detective, I want to check with
the Coroner about something.

267
00:15:18,768 --> 00:15:19,702
Yes!

268
00:15:19,769 --> 00:15:21,437
That's what I thought.

269
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:23,406
Yes, thanks.

270
00:15:23,506 --> 00:15:26,375
If you would please.
So long.

271
00:15:30,079 --> 00:15:31,013
"Charm"

272
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:32,248
Hmm...

273
00:15:32,315 --> 00:15:35,985
So that "chain of iron" was handcuffs, huh?

274
00:15:36,085 --> 00:15:40,156
Yeah.
And I keep this piece from it inside here.

275
00:15:40,323 --> 00:15:41,924
Hmm...

276
00:15:42,158 --> 00:15:44,927
Say, say! Are you two dating?

277
00:15:44,994 --> 00:15:48,998
Ah, no, no!
I'm more like an older sister to Heiji.

278
00:15:49,465 --> 00:15:52,068
More importantly,
how about you, Ran-chan?

279
00:15:52,201 --> 00:15:55,037
Are you and that
huge loves-mysteries nut going out together?

280
00:15:55,171 --> 00:15:59,408
Well, it isn't clear if you could call
our relationship that...

281
00:15:59,575 --> 00:16:03,713
We don't have the
strong bonds you and him have.

282
00:16:03,946 --> 00:16:06,916
Oi! What are you doing?

283
00:16:11,287 --> 00:16:15,191
Who's this "huge loves-mysteries nut"?

284
00:16:15,725 --> 00:16:17,026
I don't know!

285
00:16:17,126 --> 00:16:19,295
More importantly,
have you found something out?

286
00:16:19,362 --> 00:16:22,198
Hattori-kun might settle
this case first, you know.

287
00:16:22,298 --> 00:16:24,166
That's fine; it doesn't matter.

288
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,602
No matter who the detective is...

289
00:16:26,736 --> 00:16:30,639
There is always just one truth.

290
00:16:35,911 --> 00:16:39,582
Geez!
He's such a huge loves-mysteries nut!

291
00:16:39,782 --> 00:16:41,717
Ah, got it.

292
00:16:42,985 --> 00:16:44,920
Hattori-kun, it was just like you said.

293
00:16:45,121 --> 00:16:46,522
According to the Coroner...

294
00:16:46,622 --> 00:16:50,459
...there were many small cuts on the upper part
of the dead person's body from the glass...

295
00:16:50,593 --> 00:16:52,828
...and yet her clothes didn't have
any holes in them.

296
00:16:52,995 --> 00:16:54,764
I figured...

297
00:16:55,531 --> 00:16:58,034
You re-dressed Hideko-san's corpse,
didn't you?

298
00:16:58,134 --> 00:16:59,535
"Hideko-chan."

299
00:16:59,835 --> 00:17:02,605
In order to conceal your relationship
with Hideko-san.

300
00:17:02,972 --> 00:17:06,642
More than anything, you were only
thinking about protecting yourself.

301
00:17:06,876 --> 00:17:11,847
If we had been exposed,
it would have caused a lot of complications...

302
00:17:12,048 --> 00:17:14,617
But you've got to believe me!
I didn't do this!

303
00:17:14,717 --> 00:17:16,519
Then, how did the glass break?

304
00:17:16,652 --> 00:17:17,753
I don't know!

305
00:17:17,853 --> 00:17:20,289
The glass just broke on its own!

306
00:17:20,656 --> 00:17:26,395
I locked the door like always
and played the music...

307
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:28,030
"Say..."

308
00:17:28,831 --> 00:17:31,300
"...do you hear anything strange?"

309
00:17:31,667 --> 00:17:33,836
"It's just your imagination."

310
00:17:38,074 --> 00:17:41,243
Then I heard this sound like a trembling.

311
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:42,845
"Kyaa!"

312
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:45,681
A strange sound...

313
00:17:45,748 --> 00:17:48,617
Like I thought, it was...

314
00:17:48,984 --> 00:17:51,320
Like I thought, it was...

315
00:17:52,321 --> 00:17:54,657
Huh? What's that?

316
00:17:55,057 --> 00:17:57,560
Oi, oi, oi, oi!
Who gave you permission to...

317
00:17:57,626 --> 00:17:59,662
I'm MPD Investigation Unit One's
Assistant Inspector, Sato Miwako.

318
00:17:59,695 --> 00:18:01,030
MPD...

319
00:18:01,097 --> 00:18:02,698
Investigation Unit One?!

320
00:18:02,898 --> 00:18:05,968
Please excuse me! Feel free!

321
00:18:12,875 --> 00:18:17,947
When I saw the photo in this room,
I got a strange, discomforting feeling.

322
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:22,685
Look, this composition is extremely lop-sided.

323
00:18:22,818 --> 00:18:27,890
Moreover, the "No Life" has a period to it.

324
00:18:28,090 --> 00:18:30,459
And, so I thought...

325
00:18:30,893 --> 00:18:36,565
This must be part of a set of photos which
completes an English sentence.

326
00:18:36,866 --> 00:18:41,370
They're like those rival
wind god vs. lighting god pictures.

327
00:18:41,470 --> 00:18:45,841
And there's a wall that's perfect for displaying
just such a frame in the living room.

328
00:18:45,875 --> 00:18:49,011
And there was also a receipt from the store
which had handled the frame.

329
00:18:49,111 --> 00:18:50,146
"Fujimori Kazuo
Modeling Picture Frames"

330
00:18:50,179 --> 00:18:53,215
All that bothered me,
so I called Detective Sato.

331
00:18:53,315 --> 00:18:55,951
Kudo... er, Toiru-kun...

332
00:18:56,018 --> 00:18:58,154
Ah, after hearing about it from Toiru-kun...

333
00:18:58,187 --> 00:19:02,625
...I confirmed with the store that the glass
had been broken and needed to be replaced.

334
00:19:03,726 --> 00:19:05,928
That's incredible, Toiru...

335
00:19:06,262 --> 00:19:09,165
With that, the mystery of this case is solved.

336
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:13,402
Well, let's do this.

337
00:19:13,536 --> 00:19:15,638
Everyone, watch carefully.

338
00:19:38,827 --> 00:19:40,663
What's this about, Heiji?

339
00:19:40,729 --> 00:19:44,867
I only hear music and no strange sounds,
yet nothing's happening.

340
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,170
What is this?
This should be the way it went down.

341
00:19:53,409 --> 00:19:55,144
That's it...

342
00:20:15,364 --> 00:20:17,566
I guess this is it!

343
00:20:19,535 --> 00:20:23,272
Eh? Why?
Why did you lower the music?

344
00:20:23,539 --> 00:20:26,842
So now everyone, let me show you.

345
00:20:27,009 --> 00:20:29,712
There is just one truth.

346
00:20:54,336 --> 00:20:55,604
Eh?

347
00:20:55,704 --> 00:20:57,973
Is this psychic power again?

348
00:20:58,073 --> 00:20:59,375
Fool!

349
00:20:59,441 --> 00:21:01,610
That couldn't be it, now could it?

350
00:21:02,044 --> 00:21:03,746
Here goes.

351
00:21:17,993 --> 00:21:19,795
It broke...

352
00:21:20,329 --> 00:21:21,463
Why?

353
00:21:21,563 --> 00:21:23,065
You didn't do anything.

354
00:21:23,198 --> 00:21:25,167
Natural frequency...

355
00:21:25,801 --> 00:21:28,837
That's the trick that broke the glass.

356
00:21:28,904 --> 00:21:31,106
Natural frequency...

357
00:21:31,307 --> 00:21:33,509
Could it be you mean, resonance?

358
00:21:33,609 --> 00:21:34,777
That's right.

359
00:21:34,910 --> 00:21:39,848
All objects have a frequency at which
they naturally tend to vibrate at.

360
00:21:40,349 --> 00:21:42,785
The music being played in this room...

361
00:21:42,918 --> 00:21:48,290
...was set at a frequency at which only
the glass in this frame would vibrate to.

362
00:21:48,357 --> 00:21:52,294
Moreover, the trick was
a speaker hidden behind the photo...

363
00:21:52,428 --> 00:21:56,799
...that was set up to create
the sound at that frequency.

364
00:21:56,865 --> 00:22:00,602
"Sound"?
We didn't hear any sounds, did we?

365
00:22:00,736 --> 00:22:02,071
Yeah.

366
00:22:02,171 --> 00:22:03,772
Such fools...

367
00:22:03,906 --> 00:22:07,743
Anything over 20,000 hertz
and it can't be heard by average people.

368
00:22:07,843 --> 00:22:11,547
But even if people can't hear it, dogs can.

369
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:13,549
That's why...

370
00:22:15,351 --> 00:22:17,186
It became overly upset and made such a fuss.

371
00:22:17,353 --> 00:22:21,256
To a dog, it was set at an overly high volume.

372
00:22:21,390 --> 00:22:25,227
The glass in that frame
is the same as a swing in a park.

373
00:22:25,361 --> 00:22:29,498
As power is added according to
the movements of each swing...

374
00:22:29,631 --> 00:22:31,500
...the swaying becomes greater.

375
00:22:31,633 --> 00:22:33,135
In the same way...

376
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:39,007
...the glass gradually became unable to withstand
the specific frequency of those vibrations...

377
00:22:39,842 --> 00:22:42,678
...and so the glass broke.

378
00:22:42,811 --> 00:22:47,149
The criminal, using an invisible weapon,
killed Hideko-san.

379
00:22:47,349 --> 00:22:50,319
And that invisible weapon was...

380
00:22:50,853 --> 00:22:53,088
Resonance.

381
00:22:53,622 --> 00:22:55,991
Wait a minute.
I don't use that frequency.

382
00:22:56,058 --> 00:22:59,995
Thing is, this music has never broken
any glass up until now.

383
00:23:00,462 --> 00:23:02,197
Of course not.

384
00:23:02,297 --> 00:23:06,101
It was someone who knew you were always
playing this music to cover up your affair...

385
00:23:06,268 --> 00:23:10,105
...and who replaced the CD with
this specific frequency included on it.

386
00:23:10,239 --> 00:23:11,940
Right, Toiru?

387
00:23:12,174 --> 00:23:13,742
Yeah.

388
00:23:14,076 --> 00:23:15,744
The criminal is...

389
00:23:16,078 --> 00:23:17,546
...you.

390
00:23:17,780 --> 00:23:19,448
You.

391
00:23:20,916 --> 00:23:23,752
Fujimaru Yoshino-san.

392
00:23:27,523 --> 00:23:29,458
When we entered this room...

393
00:23:29,591 --> 00:23:32,661
...you pretended to stagger back
away from the photo...

394
00:23:32,761 --> 00:23:35,697
...so you could deliberately
turn down the speaker.

395
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:37,699
Detective.

396
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:40,436
Check the CD in that deck.

397
00:23:40,636 --> 00:23:43,972
The wife's fingerprints
should be all over it.

398
00:23:46,408 --> 00:23:47,943
Wait!

399
00:23:53,882 --> 00:23:55,250
Yoshino...

400
00:23:55,684 --> 00:23:57,052
Why?

401
00:23:57,419 --> 00:23:59,154
Why would you do such a thing?

402
00:24:05,294 --> 00:24:07,796
It's best if you don't repeat your crimes.

403
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:12,668
I...

404
00:24:13,302 --> 00:24:17,739
I did everything I could for you until now.

405
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:20,476
From the time I was your Assistant...

406
00:24:20,576 --> 00:24:24,046
...did you give any thought to who
gave you the idea for that music?

407
00:24:24,346 --> 00:24:26,014
The one who came up with that music was me!

408
00:24:26,114 --> 00:24:27,483
Liar!

409
00:24:28,717 --> 00:24:32,788
I'm the one who originally completed it!

410
00:24:34,289 --> 00:24:38,627
As long as it was of use to you,
I was fine with that.

411
00:24:39,161 --> 00:24:42,264
Because a man like you was in love with me.

412
00:24:42,431 --> 00:24:43,866
But...

413
00:24:44,500 --> 00:24:47,135
...that woman came in here.

414
00:24:47,236 --> 00:24:50,339
"Liar...
You've just decided this by yourself."

415
00:24:50,439 --> 00:24:56,044
"After all, him and me have been tied by
a strong bond for a long time now."

416
00:24:57,679 --> 00:24:59,515
"A bond?"

417
00:25:00,716 --> 00:25:01,750
"Bond"

418
00:25:01,783 --> 00:25:04,386
"That time you caught us?"

419
00:25:04,686 --> 00:25:06,788
"He was the one who chose that music."

420
00:25:06,955 --> 00:25:10,993
The bond I believed was between the two of us...

421
00:25:11,793 --> 00:25:14,029
I was the only one who believed in it.

422
00:25:14,496 --> 00:25:17,266
If my ball hadn't broken the windowpane...

423
00:25:17,299 --> 00:25:20,369
...Kazuo-san would still have been
on that sofa.

424
00:25:20,636 --> 00:25:21,970
Yoshino-san.

425
00:25:22,104 --> 00:25:23,972
Could it be you were trying...

426
00:25:24,206 --> 00:25:26,842
I intended to kill the both of them.

427
00:25:27,743 --> 00:25:30,112
But even if they didn't die
when the glass fell...

428
00:25:30,212 --> 00:25:34,783
...at the very least they'd suffer
serious injuries.

429
00:25:34,983 --> 00:25:39,121
Did the repairs to the frame
come from testing it beforehand?

430
00:25:39,821 --> 00:25:44,059
It was necessary to check the frequency
at which the glass would break.

431
00:25:46,028 --> 00:25:50,065
You've already seen through everything,
haven't you?

432
00:25:59,841 --> 00:26:01,643
Dear...

433
00:26:03,545 --> 00:26:05,981
Please look forward to it.

434
00:26:07,416 --> 00:26:12,487
Because I'll reveal EVERYTHING to the police.

435
00:26:14,556 --> 00:26:17,859
The two of us do have a bond!

436
00:26:19,595 --> 00:26:21,129
Damn woman...

437
00:26:21,196 --> 00:26:23,298
What bond!?

438
00:26:27,836 --> 00:26:29,538
Don't make fun of bonds...

439
00:26:29,605 --> 00:26:30,739
...because they don't come for free!

440
00:26:30,806 --> 00:26:33,075
'Cause they don't come fer free!

441
00:26:34,509 --> 00:26:37,946
You guys had better be careful too, right?

442
00:26:41,850 --> 00:26:43,719
Say, Toiru.

443
00:26:44,019 --> 00:26:47,522
When did ya start gettin'
suspicious about that wife?

444
00:26:48,757 --> 00:26:51,827
Ever since the moment she returned home...

445
00:26:52,361 --> 00:26:54,396
She made a careless remark.

446
00:26:54,463 --> 00:26:55,831
"Dear!"

447
00:26:55,998 --> 00:26:59,768
"Maybe they're so seriously hurt
they can't answer..."

448
00:26:59,835 --> 00:27:04,306
It was as if she already knew something
had happened to the two of them.

449
00:27:05,207 --> 00:27:08,543
Ah, can't take Tokyo lightly.

450
00:27:08,644 --> 00:27:13,382
First there's that Kudo whatshisname
and now this Bro as well.

451
00:27:13,515 --> 00:27:16,385
Ah... That's the thing.
Truth is...

452
00:27:16,418 --> 00:27:18,387
It really is like a swing.

453
00:27:18,453 --> 00:27:19,488
Huh?

454
00:27:19,588 --> 00:27:22,024
If you add power to match the movement...

455
00:27:22,124 --> 00:27:24,226
...it'll further increase its momentum...

456
00:27:24,359 --> 00:27:27,896
...but if you oppose the movement,
the momentum will become smaller.

457
00:27:28,130 --> 00:27:30,832
Right, Toiru-kun?

458
00:27:32,467 --> 00:27:33,869
Right.

459
00:27:37,472 --> 00:27:40,709
AH!
The game's started already!

460
00:27:40,809 --> 00:27:42,010
Kazuha, let's go!

461
00:27:42,077 --> 00:27:44,212
See ya, Ran-chan!

462
00:27:45,113 --> 00:27:50,118
Ahh! Because you didn't do it quick enough,
you failed to confess to him.

463
00:27:50,285 --> 00:27:52,387
I wonder about that guy?

464
00:27:52,654 --> 00:27:56,792
Can't take Osaka's Great Detective lightly.

465
00:27:57,025 --> 00:27:58,527
- Say, Heiji.
- Huh?

466
00:27:58,593 --> 00:28:00,362
Could it be that Toiru-kun is...

467
00:28:00,429 --> 00:28:02,330
Don't say such senseless things.

468
00:28:02,397 --> 00:28:03,632
It's okay, ain't it?

469
00:28:03,699 --> 00:28:06,268
I look forward to our next meeting.

470
00:28:06,368 --> 00:28:10,338
We'll see if he's still going with
that fool alias "Toiru" then.

471
00:28:14,643 --> 00:28:15,911
Shin'ichi!

472
00:28:16,011 --> 00:28:18,046
Glass... Adultery...

473
00:28:18,113 --> 00:28:19,681
Heiji... Ball...

474
00:28:19,748 --> 00:28:21,183
I've got it!

475
00:28:21,283 --> 00:28:23,185
I know what this is!

476
00:28:35,931 --> 00:28:37,299
"Bonds"

477
00:28:41,636 --> 00:28:44,439
Ran, thank you.

478
00:28:47,008 --> 00:28:50,946
I'm worried about the bonds between us...

479
00:28:52,380 --> 00:28:54,116
Let's hurry and go.

480
00:28:56,918 --> 00:28:58,086
- Shin'ichi!
- Ran!

481
00:28:58,186 --> 00:28:59,421
Ran!

482
00:29:00,555 --> 00:29:02,257
Damn!

483
00:29:09,664 --> 00:29:14,136
"Chat Murder Case!"

484
00:29:16,271 --> 00:29:18,607
"A Corpse That Teleports?!"

485
00:29:21,543 --> 00:29:24,279
"This Drama is Fictional"

